.TH KURVENRAUSCH 6 @PROJECT_DATE@ "kurvenrausch @PROJECT_VERSION_FULL@" "Games"
.SH NAME
kurvenrausch \- classic pseudo-3D arcade racer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kurvenrausch
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kurvenrausch
is a racer in the spirit of OutRun and Lotus Esprit Turbo Challenge: one lap
around the world in sixteen zones, from the Cote d'Azur through England, the
Netherlands, the Black Forest, the Alps, Tuscany, Egypt, Kenya, India, Korea,
Japan and the Australian outback to Arizona, the California coast, San
Francisco and the Amazon rainforest.
A second, far longer track, the Grand Tour, stops in two or three cities of
every country on the way; pick it in the pause menu's RACE SETUP.
The road forks in places into two routes that join again; keep to the side of
the road you want to take.
On the way there is traffic to pass, fuel to buy at gas stations, other cars
to choose at car dealers (stop on the forecourt and steer left or right), car
washes to clean off the mud and oil the car picks up, motels to change the
passenger, hospitals to change the driver (or patch them up after a crash),
truck stops to swap the car for a truck,
nitro to burn and, in San Francisco, crests to jump.
.PP
Without options the game opens a window and starts at the start line; the lap
clock runs from the first time the car crosses it.
With
.B \-\-screenshot
it runs headless instead: an autopilot drives for the given number of steps,
one frame is rendered and saved, and no window is opened.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start covering the whole screen instead of in a window (F11 or Alt+Enter
switches between the two).
.TP
.BI \-\-renderer " MODE"
Choose the road scene renderer: auto (GLES when available), software, or gles. F8 cycles in game.

.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " FILE"
Render headless and save the frame as a BMP image to
.IR FILE ,
then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-frames " N"
Simulate
.I N
steps (60 per second) before the screenshot.
The default is 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-position " Z"
Start the headless run at distance
.I Z
along the track.
.TP
.BI \-\-zone " N"
Start the headless run inside zone
.IR N ;
see
.BR \-\-print\-zones .
.TP
.B \-\-print\-zones
List the zones of the track with their segments and start positions, then
exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-track " N"
Drive track
.I N
for the headless run or
.BR \-\-print\-zones :
0 the Small World, 1 the Grand Tour.
.TP
.BI \-\-wav " FILE"
Also write the sound of the headless run as a WAV file.
Needs
.BR \-\-screenshot .
.TP
.BI \-\-steer " S"
Hold the steering at
.I S
(\-1 left to 1 right) instead of letting the autopilot steer.
.TP
.BI \-\-steer\-from " N"
Start holding the steering only at step
.IR N .
The default is 0.
.TP
.B \-\-horn
Hold the horn during the headless run.
.TP
.BI \-\-nitro " N"
Press nitro at step
.I N
of the headless run.
.TP
.BI \-\-fuel " L"
Start the headless run with
.I L
(0 to 1) of a tank.
.TP
.BI \-\-car " N"
Drive car model
.I N
in the headless run: 0 Spider, 1 GT Coupe, 2 Hot Hatch, 3 Muscle, 4 Big Rig,
5 Saloon, 6 Taxi, 7 Estate, 8 Patrol, 9 Racer, 10 Van, 11 Box Truck.
.TP
.B \-\-dealer
Let the autopilot pull in at the next car dealer during the headless run, and
stay there.
.TP
.BI \-\-brake " N"
From step
.I N
of the headless run on, brake (and not accelerate) to a stop, let go of the
brake for a moment, then hold it again: the car reverses.
.TP
.BI \-\-dirt " L"
Start the headless run with the car this dirty, from 0 (clean) to 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " W"
Make the screenshot
.I W
pixels wide, from 320 (4:3) to 640, at 240 pixels high: the picture as on a
wide screen.
.TP
.B \-\-wash
Let the autopilot pull in at the next car wash during the headless run, and
stay there.
.TP
.BI \-\-visit " KIND"
Let the autopilot pull in at the next lot of
.I KIND
during the headless run, and stay there:
.B gas
(a gas station),
.B dealer
(everyday cars),
.B sports
(sports cars),
.BR wash ,
.BR motel ,
.BR hospital ,
.BR truckstop ,
.B chemical
(nitro) or
.B garage
(your own, before the start line).
.TP
.B \-\-pause
Show the pause menu in the screenshot.
.TP
.BI \-\-menu " PAGE"
Show this page of the pause menu in the screenshot: pause, race, options,
gameplay, video, audio, controls, keyboard, gamepad, extras, records or
debug.
.TP
.BI \-\-signal " N"
Switch the indicators on for the headless run: \-1 left, 1 right, 2 the
hazard lights.
.TP
.B \-\-headlights
Switch the headlights on for the headless run.
.TP
.B \-\-attract
Show the attract mode in the screenshot: the camera following a car of the
traffic, as the game does when it starts and when nobody plays.
.TP
.BI \-\-hour " H"
Start the headless run at
.I H
o'clock (0 to 24); the day passes in eight minutes.
.TP
.BI \-\-touch " X,Y"
Hold a finger on the touch screen at
.IR X , Y
(framebuffer pixels, 320\(mu240) all through the headless run; may be given
several times. The touch controls show in the screenshot.
.TP
.BI \-\-police " N"
Start a police chase at step
.I N
of the headless run.
.TP
.BI \-\-music " N"
Play the radio's track
.I N
(0 to 2) in the
.B \-\-wav
recording; without, the recording has no music.
.TP
.BI \-\-storm " L"
Hold the weather of the headless run at
.IR L ,
from 0 (clear) to 1 (a storm), instead of letting it drift.
.TP
.BI \-\-view " N"
Render the headless run from camera view
.IR N :
0 chase, 1 far, 2 bumper, 3 cockpit.
.TP
.BI \-\-handbrake " N"
Hold the handbrake from step
.I N
of the headless run on.
.TP
.BI \-\-icon " FILE"
Write the application icon (32\(mu32 pixels) as a BMP image to
.IR FILE ,
then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-sprites
Browse every sprite of the game in a window (left and right step through
them, up and down through the categories), then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH CONTROLS
.TS
l l l.
Keyboard	Gamepad	Action
\(ua or W	right trigger, A	accelerate
\(da or S	left trigger, B	brake; stopped, let go and press again: reverse
\(<- \(-> or A D	left stick, D\-pad	steer
Ctrl	left shoulder	handbrake
H	X	horn
Space	Y, right shoulder	nitro
P	Start	pause menu
R		restart
C	Back	camera view: chase, far, bumper, cockpit
N	right stick flicked up	radio: the next track, or off
B	right stick flicked down	radio: the previous track
L	D\-pad up	headlights on or off
Q E	right stick flicked left, right	indicator left, right (again: off)
Z	D\-pad down	hazard lights
Tab	right stick click	mini map: around the car or the whole lap
M		mute the sound
F11, Alt+Enter		toggle fullscreen
Esc		pause; in the pause menu, back a page (Quit is a menu item on native builds)
.TE
.PP
All but Esc, F8, F11 and Start can be rebound in the pause menu's
OPTIONS \(-> CONTROLS, two keys and two pad inputs per action.
.PP
The pause menu: RESUME, RESTART, RACE SETUP (track, start country, time of
day, weather, traffic), OPTIONS (GAMEPLAY, VIDEO, AUDIO, CONTROLS, DEBUG),
EXTRAS (the demo, lap records) and, on native builds, QUIT.
Arrow keys or D\-pad move, Enter or A picks, left and right change a
setting, Esc or B go back; the mouse works too.
Everything set there is kept for the next run.
.PP
Any game controller SDL knows works and can be plugged in at any time.
Sticks and triggers are analog; keyboard and gamepad can be used together.
The pad rumbles on crashes, scraping a barrier, close passes, nitro and when
leaving the road.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG
Additional game controller mappings, in SDL's format.
.TP
.BR SDL_VIDEODRIVER ", " SDL_AUDIODRIVER
Select SDL's video and audio drivers, for example
.B dummy
to run without a display or sound device.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Where the game keeps its state, see
.BR FILES ;
unset, empty or not an absolute path, it is
.IR ~/.local/state .
.SH FILES
The game remembers between runs, in
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/kurvenrausch/ ;
headless runs neither read nor write these:
.TP
.I choices
The car, driver and passenger chosen last, picked up again on the next start.
.TP
.I laps.tsv
Every lap completed, one per line: the time (UTC), the lap time in seconds,
the car, the driver and the passenger, separated by tabs.
The fastest of them is the record shown as BEST.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if the window could not be opened, an option is unknown,
incomplete or needs
.B \-\-screenshot
with it, or a file could not be written.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render the start of the Tuscany zone after two and a half seconds:
.PP
.EX
kurvenrausch \-\-screenshot shot.bmp \-\-zone 3 \-\-frames 150
.EE
.PP
Record most of a lap with its sound:
.PP
.EX
kurvenrausch \-\-screenshot shot.bmp \-\-frames 9000 \-\-wav lap.wav
.EE
